\caption(Reconstruction copies selected vectors as encoder derivatives and gives zero book derivatives. Dictionary and commitment routes affect opposite parameter groups; the book's unused middle entry has zero derivative.)
\alttext(Two blue encoder points connect to the selected outer red dictionary points. The point at minus one-half lies exactly between dictionary entries minus one and zero; the lower-index entry is chosen.)

> Native data and the complete fitting program

Offline beta-vae-assets preparation produces all 294 binary 28×28 circle/square images:
2 shapes×3 sizes×7 x-positions×7 y-positions. Radius=size+2 and centre=(3x+5,3y+5), with
inclusive Euclidean boundaries for circles and inclusive Chebyshev boundaries for squares.
Residue (x+2y+size+3shape) mod 7 assigns test=0, validation=1 and fit=2–6, giving disjoint
210/42/42 factor combinations. These small procedural images are not a downloaded benchmark.
Factor labels never enter the model, optimizer or checkpoint criterion.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n      = dm::nn;
  const auto cache = dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets");
  const auto a     = n::load_npz((std::filesystem::path(cache) / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  auto       find  = [&](const std::string& name) {
    for (const auto& [key, value] : a)
      if (key == name)
        return value;
    throw std::runtime_error(name);
  };
  std::print("| pool | images | geometry | factor columns |\n|---|---:|---|---:|\n");
  for (const std::string split : {"fit", "validation", "test"})
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | 28x28x1 | {} |\n",
        split,
        find(split + "_images").size(0),
        find(split + "_factors").size(1));
}
```
