All fourteen archives/759,770 array values and complete batch/history TSV files reproduce
the frozen original source exactly. Two summary MSEs now use tensor Float64 reductions
instead of host accumulation; observed roundoff is below 3e-14. All other non-timing JSON
values remain exact. The program verifies discrete-only decoding, fixed repeats, single/batch
parity, invalid IDs and parameter immutability during inference/prior fitting.

> Checkpoint selection and training observations

The blue trace averages pre-update training objectives across the parameter path within an
epoch. Red validation NLL uses the completed epoch's parameters and excludes latent penalties.
These are different observations and objectives; their gap alone does not measure overfitting.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vq_vae_validation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::ifstream input("build/vq_vae/history.tsv");
  std::string   header;
  std::getline(input, header);
  std::vector<double> e, train, val;
  double              epoch, t, n, d, c, l;
  while (input >> epoch >> t >> n >> d >> c >> l) {
    e.push_back(epoch);
    train.push_back(t);
    val.push_back(n);
  }
  if (e.size() != 3)
    return 1;
  auto chart = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  chart.lines(e, train, "train (pre)", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(e, train, "", dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .lines(e, val, "val NLL (end)", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .points(e, val, "", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .title("Training objective and validation reconstruction NLL")
      .x_label("completed epoch / all three eligible")
      .y_label("nats plus latent penalties where included")
      .x_ticks({1, 2, 3}, {"1", "2", "3"})
      .save_svg("build/vq_vae_validation.svg");
}
